  "body": "Follow-up from #383 (PR #478).\n\n**Today:** the Machines pane edits a machine on its raw JSON and keeps unknown keys, but saving writes the keys sorted alphabetically. The workspace `serde_json` is built without `preserve_order`. The content round-trips exactly; a hand-written file's layout and diff readability don't.\n\n**Options:**\n1. Turn on `serde_json/preserve_order` workspace-wide. This changes every JSON writer, project files included, so it needs a project-file byte-stability check, since key order is part of the project round-trip pins.\n2. Keep it local: write `.mch` files through an order-keeping path (e.g. `indexmap`-backed values for this writer only).\n\n**Done means:** an edited and saved `.mch` keeps its original key order (new keys appended), pinned by a round-trip test; project files stay byte-identical.",
